<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24897" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">īrĭnus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴρινος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the plant iris</i>, <i>iris-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sucus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					30, 14, 43, § 142</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">unguentum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					5, 18, 8</span></i>
			. — Hence, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">īrĭnum</span></b> ,
				i, n., <i>ointment made
				from the iris</i>, <i>iris-ointment</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 3,
			18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 20, 17, 71, §
		182</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
